to make this sheet look nice.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.540
So we'll not go over all the key steps,

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.310
but I do want us to do a
couple of basic things.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.180
And this is really just basic
formatting because you'll see

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.650
that there are all kinds of font types

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.520
and font sizes used here.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.940
So let's start by
highlighting the whole sheet,

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.910
and you do that by control +
A to highlight just the table.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.210
But then if you press A once again,

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.090
it highlights the full sheet.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.710
Now what I do is, I usually
keep to do this manually.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:20.280
So just type in here Arial
and also type in here

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.740
the font size 10.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.190
And let's move to moving in the sheet,

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.450
because what I think is extremely crucial

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.710
is how you navigate around.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.740
And of course, with the arrow
keys you can navigate here

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.890
in the five of this, always
takes quite a lot of time

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.040
that's not really effective.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.570
And one very key movement
that you will literally use

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.750
all the time is pressing the control key

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.360
and then moving the arrow key.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:46.150
So now I move control + arrow
down, control + arrow right,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.280
Control + arrow up, control + arrow left.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.113
So if you do this,

00:04:50.113 --> 00:04:53.140
you can very quickly move
over the whole table.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.040
This is just the shortcut
that you will use

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.190
in combination with all
other kinds of things,

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.720
just to navigate your way around the table

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.490
in a quick and direct way.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.420
Next is about highlighting cells.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.700
And many beginners, what they will do,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.840
is likely they will just take the mouse,

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.910
highlight it, press down and
then move down like this.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.410
And if the table isn't too long

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.120
with 170 lines or rows or
so, this will even work.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.150
But if you have a table
with several thousand rows,

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.910
this can take you minutes
until you have scrolled down

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:22.830
in this manner.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.030
So this is not what you do,

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.200
and instead you use your
keyboard once again.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.020
And specifically you press shift + control

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.420
and then arrow down.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.390
If you start here, shift
+ control + arrow down

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.220
to really highlight the
full area of the table.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.600
Of course, then you can expand that

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.460
if you then press the right arrow button,

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.820
while you still have shift
and control knocked down,

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.380
then you can have it all marked,

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.220
or now I press up and it has
only the first one marked.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.053
Now that being said,

00:05:48.053 --> 00:05:50.160
let's imagine you would
want to format here

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.600
this purchasing price area
with a proper number format

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.520
using for instance, also currency icon.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.160
So here again, we would do exactly this.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.920
So shift + control + down to mark this,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.150
and now we want to open
the format cells menu.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:08.270
And how this works is
you press control + 1

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.610
to open this format sales menu.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.370
So here let's imagine this
is Great British Pounds.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.500
Then you would insert
here counting, press okay,

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.890
and now you have it all highlighted

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.100
in this accounting format.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.580
We can do the same thing
for the quantity as well.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.750
Let's highlight this press control + 1,

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:30.730
press now the number format
with this separate icon.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:33.050
And now it's all in such a format as well.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.870
Another shortcut that you
will super frequently use

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:39.390
is to highlight whole rows or columns.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.890
And again, the beginner
might do that with the mouse.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.700
You might click here on
different rows or columns

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.350
to highlight them, but of
course the overall goal

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.010
of a skilled practitioner in Excel

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.770
is to use the mouse as rarely as possible.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:54.340
So we want to do that
with our keyboard as well.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:56.080
And indeed, if you want
to highlight a row,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.000
what you need to do first is to navigate

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.600
with the cursor icon to the
role that you want to highlight

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.990
and then you just press shift + space

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.220
to highlight the row.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.350
And indeed, if you want
to highlight a column,

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:11.040
you press control + space
to highlight the column.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.990
So it's shift + space for the rows

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.920
and control + space for the columns.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.370
And another way that
you can use that really

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.860
if you present the model,
if you have this model,

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.190
for instance, projected
with a beamer to a wall,

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.630
and you're showing something,

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.990
sometimes it can be difficult
to really follow your cursor

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.730
because it's not that like
visible, not that bold,

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:30.810
not that in your face.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.500
But if you want to talk
about a specific number

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.890
you want to highlight that.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.740
A little thing that you can do

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.240
is to just highlight the whole row.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.700
And then here, you always see
the field already highlighted

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.250
that you have the cursor in.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.520
This really helps and the
person who was watching this,

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.560
who's sitting there with you in the room,

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.580
just to see where exactly
you are in the table.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.577
Very much related to this

00:07:50.577 --> 00:07:54.310
is now to insert new rows or new columns.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.660
And here what you do is you
first highlight for instance,

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.140
the row, and then you
press control and plus

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:04.300
to insert a new row in
this case above that.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.670
So we're gonna highlight it first.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.190
So highlight the row
and then control + plus

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:11.820
to have a new row inserted above that.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.660
And of cause, very similarly
it then works with the columns.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.920
So first highlight the
column and then again,

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.870
you press the same thing.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:21.050
So control + plus to
then insert a new column.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.060
So depending on what
was highlighted first,

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.900
whether it was a row or
a column, control + plus

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:29.460
will insert then accordingly
a row or a column.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.850
This works the other way around as well.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.750
So if you want to delete a row or column,

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.610
you need to highlight
the row or the column

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.780
that you want to have deleted,

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.003
and then you need to press control+ minus.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:43.120
So in this case to delete,
really the columns,

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.980
or your press control + minus
to then delete the rows.

